      "code": "5.3",
      "title": "Electron & Molecular Geometry (PhET)",
      "concept": {
        "summary": "Domain (electron group): any region of electrons around the central atom.",
        "keyIdeas": [
          "Each bond is ONE domain, whether it is single, double or triple. Each lone pair is ONE domain.",
          "Domains = bonding pairs + lone pairs. Electron geometry counts every domain; molecular geometry names only where the atoms are."
        ]
      },
      "directions": "Open PhET Molecule Shapes (phet.colorado.edu) and choose Model. Check Show Lone Pairs, Show Bond Angles, Electron Geometry and Molecule Geometry. For each row, add single bonds to match the bonding pairs, then add lone pairs until the total matches the domains. Record the lone pairs, both shape names and the bond angle(s). Press Remove All before the next row.",
